WEBVTT

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.510
<i>It's strange...</i>

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.150
<i>There's someone out there
who knows Gramps' sound.</i>

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.860
<i>Just knowing that...</i>

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.260
<i>...makes my chest feel tight.</i>

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.240
Gramps!

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.210
Why won't you teach me it?

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:21.720
It's not just you. I'm not
teaching that piece to anyone.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.380
Sound.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:26.110
Use your own sound to steal it.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:50.530
Those Snow

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:50.530
White Notes

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.510
Ta

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.510
nukichi

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.510
Diner

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:03.510
Episode 4
Spring Dawn

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:05.310
Dokkoi, you sure look happy!

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.830
Ah, Setsu-san! Welcome back.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.730
If someone seems down,
it's because they're hungry!

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.080
Hello, Sawamura speaking.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.240
<i>It's me.</i>

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.680
Oh, Setsu. What's up?

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:31.820
Me?

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.270
I just got home from playing at a shop.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:36.830
I'm eating now. Cup ramen.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.210
They'll get soggy.
Mind if I eat while we talk?

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.800
Huh? What was that?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.250
I couldn't hear you.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.400
Say it again.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.760
<i>"Shungyou."</i>

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.270
<i>I want you to find a tape of Gramps
playing "Shungyou,"</i>

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.840
<i>and send it to me right away.</i>

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.500
<i>You gonna play it?</i>

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:54.680
Yeah.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.820
<i>You really think you can play it?</i>

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.570
Of course I don't.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:04.160
The way Gramps played, it was like he
had ten or twenty fingers on his left hand.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.540
No way can I play like that.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.710
<i>What made you want to play it, then?</i>

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:12.080
This girl's grandmother knows the refrain
from Gramps' "Shungyou."

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.590
Her grandmother really
wants to hear it again,

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.330
and this girl's desperate to make it happen.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:24.430
If they got their hopes up and I ended up
not living up to them, it'd kill me.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.860
<i>What?</i>

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:29.600
<i>So the reason he looked down
is because of a girl he likes?</i>

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.890
<i>Setsu, you're hilarious.</i>

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:34.110
What?

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:35.910
It's not funny.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.590
<i>Listen to me.</i>

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.170
<i>You know Gramps, and you know
how difficult his "Shungyou" is.</i>

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.110
<i>This girl and her grandma don't.</i>

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.240
She's only thinking about how her
grandma wants to hear it again.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:53.290
But in your case, you might know the girl,

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.800
but you have no idea
how her grandmother feels.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:01.420
This girl didn't know Gramps.
You don't know her grandma.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:06.330
The strength of feeling is the difference
between knowing and not knowing.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.320
So don't be so scared of playing it.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.840
You should let her grandma
hear your "Shungyou."

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:18.510
<i>Just add yourself into her
grandma's memory of Gramps.</i>

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.710
<i>Say: "This is what
'Shungyou' sounds like now."</i>

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:22.540
<i>Go rewrite her memory.</i>

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.240
Hey, Wakana-chan.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.130
<i>Yeah?</i>

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:32.250
What kind of song was "Jongara Bushi" again?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.480
What? Why would you ask me that now?

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.050
Let's see, it goes...

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.800
Wakana-chan. I'm sorry.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.480
I gave a really bad performance
in front of Kamiki Seiryuu.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.550
You disgraced yourself in front of that guy?

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.450
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.170
In front of that smug Tokyo jerk?

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:02.990
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.480
<i>Anyone who goes off
half-cocked like that can go die!</i>

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.740
Man. They're all soggy now.

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:14.590
There's no need to say "go die."

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:17.220
Rice balls?

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.420
Help yourself

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:19.880
"Help yourself"?

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.250
Help yourself

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.960
So I can just take them?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.640
<i>Th-They're not poisoned... are they?</i>

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:29.210
You're so beautiful...

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.470
...my Kiyora 2.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:39.480
Hello?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.450
How come you met up with Sawamura Setsu?

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:45.160
And if you saw him yesterday,
why'd you only text me about it today?

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.160
<i>He's really nothing like Wakana-kun, is he?</i>

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.000
You didn't answer my question!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.690
<i>He came to my show, so I got him
to play for me in my dressing room.</i>

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:54.980
You're kidding! For real?

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.460
<i>It was kind of disappointing.</i>

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:57.240
What?

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.000
Maybe he hasn't been playing
the shamisen over there.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.410
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.520
<i>He wasn't able to show me his "sound."</i>

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:09.610
Dragging Setsu-kun out of
his shell is going to be tough.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:13.800
Though, if that ever happens,
he'll be utterly terrifying.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.400
<i>You got all that from one
"disappointing" performance?</i>

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.400
It was enough to get a sense of his potential.

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:24.060
He won't be able to develop
his sound by himself.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:27.440
He's the type that grows through
the people who listen to him.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.450
Ta

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.450
nukichi

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.450
Diner

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.370
I don't know
who you are,
but thank you.
It was delicious.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.370
He ate them.

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:39.620
I'm so glad.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:44.730
What's that?

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:46.560
The song Maeda-san's looking for.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:50.220
But there's one slight problem.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.000
Huh?

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:54.270
You're a lucky guy, you know that?

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.980
I just happen to be an audiophile.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:59.800
No one listens to cassettes these days.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:00.760
You rich?

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.720
I'm not the one with the money.
My parents are.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.170
I have no idea what they do, though.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:08.690
I just had a thought.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:11.660
Couldn't you just play
this tape for her grandma?

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.560
Didn't you learn anything
from the show the other day?

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:14.950
Huh?

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:18.600
The are is completely
different when it's played live.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:22.620
Maeda-san wants her grandmother
to hear it played in person,

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.630
because she wants her
to experience that, right?

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:27.580
Well, that's true.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.090
Just find yourself a seat.

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:32.870
Here we go.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.140
Hey...

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:43.640
When Kamiki Seiryuu said he wanted to
test our skills, why'd he make you play?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:44.480
Shhh!

00:08:58.490 --> 00:08:59.850
<i>Waves?</i>

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.180
<i>No... Is it the wind?</i>

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:55.710
<i>Here it is!</i>

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:57.570
<i>Right around here...</i>

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.610
<i>I love this part.</i>

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:03.490
<i>Listen.</i>

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.090
<i>The picking's insanely fast.</i>

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:31.640
<i>Is he really playing this all by himself?</i>

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:56.510
Spring dawn.

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:01.840
Your grandpa was amazing.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.610
That wasn't human.

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:06.480
Even a layman like me
can tell he had godly skills.

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:09.910
That's why I'm not sure what to do.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:23.730
<i>You should let her grandma
hear your "Shungyou."</i>

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:35.230
<i>My fingers and my bachi just can't keep up!</i>

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:38.250
That furrowed brow is <i>so</i> not a good look.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:41.380
Your song was so sharp
and pointy, it pained me.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.000
It "pained" you?

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.350
So I'll give you this.

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:48.390
I made it: a little, round Tamapiyo chick!

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.680
With these types of things,

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:54.540
the simpler they are, the more
expressions you see in them.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:57.280
Before you know it, your heart
skips a beat, you know?

00:11:58.170 --> 00:11:59.910
Just look at what a cutie he is.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.660
They're super popular
'cause anyone can make them.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.120
Even fat-fingered types.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.480
Oh, dear. That wasn't a dig, you know.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:10.670
Bye now!

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:21.670
He's amazing!

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.720
You said you saw him play "live."
This is what you meant?

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.010
It was live. A livestream.

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:28.650
I can't believe you.

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:29.630
Can't believe what?

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.410
Why didn't you say anything to Shuri?

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.660
You could've told her
Sawamura plays the shamisen.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:37.390
So <i>I</i> should've said something
even though <i>he</i> didn't?

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:40.590
He probably didn't want to bring it up.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.680
I mean, that song <i>is</i> super difficult.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:46.360
After hearing him play that show,
I could tell it'd be easy for him.

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:48.800
So why didn't you say anything?!

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:51.470
You know how desperate
Shuri is to help her grandma!

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.950
There's no need to put it like that! I know

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:57.210
You just enjoyed putting Shuri
in a difficult position, didn't you?!

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:04.630
Kaito!

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:07.590
Shuri's all you ever think about!

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:35.760
<i>Gramps has always been
my guide and my goal.</i>

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.920
<i>But there's no way I can ever be him.</i>

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:43.470
<i>Which means...</i>

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:48.620
<i>...one by one, I have to cast
aside all of Gramps' sounds.</i>

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:54.020
<i>I'll peel it all away.</i>

00:13:54.670 --> 00:13:57.880
<i>I'll steal Gramps' "Shungyou"...</i>

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:03.070
<i>And my sound will...</i>

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.330
Oh.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.710
It's turned out too simple.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.340
I wonder if it's still worth listening to.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:21.360
Here you are!

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.130
Make sure you eat lots, okay?

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:27.390
Oh, Rai-san. Hello!

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:28.600
Hi!

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.630
Oh, you know Rai-san?

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:35.550
No, I wouldn't say we
"know" each other, exactly...

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:37.560
A hosozao shamisen?

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:39.170
Good work today.

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:40.060
Thanks.

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.780
Rai-san is Yonefuku-san's son.

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:47.660
Yonefuku-san is a rakugo entertainer.
He's your neighbor across the hall.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:48.940
Nice to meet you.

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:50.490
Oh, um... It's my pleasure.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.430
Sakura-chan.

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:54.600
I'll have the grilled fish set, too, please.

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:55.740
Coming right up!

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.490
Um, about earlier...

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.250
Your face looks less pinched.

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:02.330
Thanks to you.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.420
It'll get cold. You should hurry up and eat.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:14.050
Can't we do this in Grandma's room?

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:16.040
Not musical instruments.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:19.520
The sound might travel and
frighten some of our residents.

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:25.130
What's eating you two?
You could've just not come.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:27.390
I-I want to be here, really!

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.500
Here we are.

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:31.860
Grandma!

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:36.800
Grandma, you'll get to listen today
to that song you wanted to hear again.

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:38.450
Right, Sawamura-kun?

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.120
Should I start playing now?

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:45.140
Are you alive?

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.080
I'm alive!

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:52.680
Grandma, make sure you don't
drop dead on me before I finish.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:55.090
You're being really rude, you know.

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:59.190
<i>This is someone who's remembered
Gramps' sound for a long time.</i>

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.080
<i>Will you teach me?</i>

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:05.100
<i>What did Gramps feel that allowed
him to create his "Shungyou"?</i>

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:07.990
<i>Hey, Gramps.</i>

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:12.190
<i>This person only knows
your sound from long ago.</i>

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:13.390
<i>Can I entrust her with this?</i>

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:18.250
<i>With this piece that will be
my guidepost from now on?</i>

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:22.510
Impromptu piece: "Shungyou (Spring Dawn)."

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:24.310
I humbly ask for your kind attention.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.530
<i>Oh, yes, that's right...</i>

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:50.900
<i>When I was six years old,
I was evacuated to the countryside.</i>

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.820
<i>My distant relatives were cold to me.</i>

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:59.800
<i>Those times were terribly
painful. I was so lonely.</i>

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:04.830
<i>Even now, my memories of those days</i>

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:13.040
<i>flow slowly through my mind over
and over again, without sound or color.</i>

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:20.910
<i>Do you want to hear about those times?</i>

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:29.530
<i>The phrase Grandma used to sing!</i>

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:36.510
<i>That young man came through the snow.</i>

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:39.270
<i>Such poor visibility.</i>

00:17:39.270 --> 00:17:42.700
<i>A humble man with a humble shamisen.</i>

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:47.210
<i>He was twelve or thirteen.</i>

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:51.500
<i>He only managed to play two or three songs.</i>

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:55.720
<i>"Our country suffers so,
and here you are begging?"</i>

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:58.810
<i>No one listened to him.</i>

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:11.770
<i>He stayed in another family's
shed for roughly three days.</i>

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.400
<i>They'd allowed him to wait
out the snowstorm there.</i>

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.910
<i>"Please play the shamisen for me," I said,</i>

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.990
<i>and gave him a potato
I'd saved from my rations.</i>

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:28.510
<i>So he did. He played me
a song with no name.</i>

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:37.640
Onii-chan, what's wrong?

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.340
The potato was so delicious...

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:45.050
but it was supposed to be your food.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:47.450
You must be so hungry.

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:53.480
Onii-chan, Toshiko's dad died.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:57.040
So it's fine if Toshiko dies, too.

00:18:58.410 --> 00:18:59.370
No.

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:03.420
You have to live.

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:29.640
<i>Grandma...</i>

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:31.570
<i>Grandma's smiling!</i>

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:40.800
<i>He took all that sound and simplified it
this much so he could play it for us.</i>

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:44.140
<i>I love it.</i>

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.160
<i>A spring dawn.</i>

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.000
<i>The cold eases.</i>

00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:57.820
<i>When the darkness
dissolves into light...</i>

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:02.430
<i>What do you see in that moment?</i>

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:28.570
<i>If Kamiki Seiryuu's sound
is the sound of a giant bell,</i>

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:31.580
<i>Sawamura's sound is the sound of a heart.</i>

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:55.310
That's not it.

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:58.990
It's completely different.

00:20:58.990 --> 00:21:01.850
It's nothing like what I heard.

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:05.170
Then, it wasn't... right.

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:08.570
There's no need to say that, Grandma.

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:11.320
Your sound when you play is very good.

00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:14.380
Good? Me?

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:19.380
What I heard back then was a humble sound.

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:22.940
What you heard then was only the beginning.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:26.890
Gramps spent thirty years
perfecting this piece.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:30.640
And this year, he passed away.

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:36.360
Was he playing all the way to the end?

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:37.120
Yeah.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:42.080
Then, the shamisen he played in order to live

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:44.650
ended up giving him life instead.

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:51.280
The shamisen he had wasn't
nearly as fine as yours.

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:55.180
It was smaller and the skin was ripped.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:22:00.790
He'd tied his broken strings together,
saying it was fine as long as they made a noise.

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:03.400
I only play so I can eat.

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:05.740
You have to live.

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:09.730
Onii-chan, I...

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:14.010
I went through a lot after that,

00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:17.140
but I'm so glad I kept on living.

00:22:19.070 --> 00:22:23.410
The quality of his sound was so gentle.

00:22:23.410 --> 00:22:26.360
It gave you the courage to live.

00:22:27.250 --> 00:22:32.370
Your sound holds a gentleness
that can heal people's pain.

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:36.280
You inherited the living
spirit of his sound, didn't you?

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:41.870
Having the past connect with the
present like this makes me so happy.

00:22:41.870 --> 00:22:43.630
Thank you.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:47.640
It was my pleasure. Thank you very much.

00:22:49.910 --> 00:22:52.480
I'm not afraid to sleep.

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:55.960
From now on, I'll be able
to have some good dreams.

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:02.790
It's been a long time since
Grandma talked that much.

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:04.770
She was just like her old self.

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:05.770
I'm happy for you.

00:23:05.770 --> 00:23:06.780
Thanks.

00:23:09.710 --> 00:23:10.950
Sawamura-kun!

00:23:14.270 --> 00:23:15.530
Thank you.

00:23:17.650 --> 00:23:18.460
Sure.

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:20.320
You're so curt.

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:24.140
So you've accomplished your goal now.

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:26.540
What are you going to do about
the Tsugaru Shamisen Club?

00:23:28.060 --> 00:23:29.050
Keep it going!

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:31.350
After all, everyone here's joining.

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:31.860
Huh?

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:34.080
And with Sawamura-kun,
we'll have the strength of a hundred!

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:34.950
What?

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:36.060
Why me?

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:38.590
I'll ask Koyabu-sensei to be our advisor.

00:23:38.590 --> 00:23:39.640
I can't do that!

00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:40.850
No running away now.

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:43.280
<i>What's going to happen with all this?</i>

00:23:54.600 --> 00:23:56.310
That feels so good.

00:23:56.310 --> 00:23:57.310
President.

00:23:57.820 --> 00:23:59.220
What is it?

00:23:59.220 --> 00:24:03.100
We've received a report from the unit
keeping an eye on Setsu-san in Japan.

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:04.590
Read it for me.

00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:10.690
The son, Setsu, has joined his high school's
Tsugaru Shamisen Appreciation Club.

00:24:11.350 --> 00:24:14.480
Okay. Time to iron out the details of our plan.

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:15.760
Roger.

00:24:20.380 --> 00:24:21.680
Setsu.

